  "reason": "We have one data point: RNA-only with PCA (single profile) achieves ~48.5% accuracy, which is a weak baseline. The most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task at all. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean single-modality baseline that directly answers: 'Does the image channel provide complementary or superior information?' This is the foundational question for a multimodal study. If image-only is competitive or better, it justifies investing remaining budget in multimodal fusion configs; if it is poor, we should focus on improving RNA representations (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation. ResNet50 is a standard, reliable encoder, making this a fair test of the image modality's intrinsic value. This experiment isolates one key design axis (modality) while holding profile setting at singleprofile, enabling a direct comparison with the RNA baseline."
